 operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-5{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-5$ times the third row to the first row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-5{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}5+(-5)(1) & 3+(-5)(0) & 6+(-5)(3) \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186525169 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -22 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525170 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525173 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525183 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525189 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 9 & -6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525181 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$ on $X?$"] [17592186525181 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & 0+(-3)(-8) & 0+(-3)(6) \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 24 & -18 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186525175 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -11 & 6\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525179 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 24 & -18 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525180 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & -18\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525187 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525193 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525191 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ on $M?$"] [17592186525191 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -2+(3)(5) & 7+(3)(3) \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 16 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186525164 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 16 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525172 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525184 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525186 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186525188 :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [17592186059581 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ on $A?$"] [17592186059581 :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059956 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ on $M?$"] [17592186059956 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5+(-1)(5) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(-1) & 1+(-1)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186236231 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186236337 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186236920 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186237177 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 9 & 1\\end{