:answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264448 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264641 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}6 & 5 & -6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 9 \\\\ -1 & -9 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186265812 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186265812 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4+(-1)(-1) & 4+(-1)(9) & 6+(-1)(-2) & 7+(-1)(6) \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186263962 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & 9 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264202 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264355 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 9 & -7 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 5 & 7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264672 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186264841 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}9 & 0 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 6 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 9 & -2 & 6\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186341857 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $M?$"] [17592186341857 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & -1+(-1)(0) & 1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(3)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186339758 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186339797 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186340679 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186340698 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186341011 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 & 2\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186341863 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $U?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186341863 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0+0 & -1+1 & -3+0 & 4+3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186339173 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186339802 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186339971 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186340069 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 10\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186340394 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -7\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388069 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$"] [17592186388069 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $-\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $-\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{3}:=(-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 6 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot (-3) & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 9 & (-\\frac{1}{3})\\cdot 0\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186388071 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & -\\frac{8}{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388072 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -3 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388073 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388074 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186388075 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -9 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 9 & 0\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393222 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ on $T?$"] [17592186393222 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $2$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ -2+(2)(1) & -2+(2)(3) & 1+(2)(2)\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186393224 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393225 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -4\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393226 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393227 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393228 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393229 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $X?$"] [17592186393229 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & 5+(-1)(3) & -1+(-1)(2) & 2+(-1)(1) \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186393231 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393232 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393233 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393234 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393235 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 3 & -2\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393236 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $N,$ given by\n\n$$\nN=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ on $N?$"] [17592186393236 :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2+(-2)(1) & 1+(-2)(-2) & 2+(-2)(1) & 3+(-2)(-1) \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186393238 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393239 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393240 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393241 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186393242 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186409514 :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $V,$ given by\n\n$$\nV=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $V?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186409514 :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ means that we need to swap the second and third rows.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1+(-1)(1) & -1+(-1)(0) & 0+(-1)(0) & 3+(-1)(2) \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186409502 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186409503 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186409504 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186409509 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186409510 :answer/value "\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]"] [17592186059582 :question/problem "Which elementary row operation could transform the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n"] [17592186059582 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has been changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nNow, applying the operation $R_2:=R_2+1 \\cdot R_1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+1\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 4+1\\cdot (-4) & 1+1\\cdot (-2) & 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation could be done by the operation \n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+1\\cdot R_1\n$$\n\nor simply\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+R_1.\n$$"] [17592186060199 :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -14\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -14\\end{bmatrix}\n$$?"] [17592186057655 :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + R_{3}"] [17592186057656 :answer/value "R_{1}:=R_{1} + \\frac{1}{4}R_{2}"] [17592186057657 :answer/value "R_{2}:=\\frac{1}{4}R_{2}"] [17592186057658 :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-3)R_{1}"] [17592186057659 :answer/value "R_{1}↔R_{2}"] [17592186060203 :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $Y$, where\n$$\nX = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nY = \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$?"] [17592186057679 :answer/value "R_{3}:=R_{3} + (-3)R_{1}"] [17592186057680 :answer/value "R_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}R_{3}"] [17592186057681 :answer/value "R_{1}↔R_{3}"] [17592186057682 :answer/value "R_{1}↔R_{2}"] [17592186057683 :answer/value "R_{2}:=R_{2} + 3R_{1}"] [17592186265820 :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $A$ into the matrix $B$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$"] [17592186265820 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the $1$st and the $2$nd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 10 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}.\n$$"] [17592186263254 :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{1}"] [17592186263822 :answer/value "{R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot {R}_{3}"] [17592186264042 :answer/value "{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}"] [17592186264244 :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}"] [17592186264958 :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{10})\\cdot {R}_{3}"] [17592186265822 :question/problem "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix  $C$ into the matrix $D$, where \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 