m of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $x_3=5.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(5)=-2\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_2=-2-5=-7.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute both $x_3 = 5$ and $x_2 = -7$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx_1+(-7)-(5) = 1\n\t\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n\tx_1 = 1 + 7 + 5 = 13.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x_1 = 13,$ $x_2=-7,$ and $x_3 = 5.$ Or, in vector form, the solution is $\\langle 13,-7,5 \\rangle.$"] [17592186096925 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186096925 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+y+z &=1 \\\\ y+z &=1 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that $z=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,y=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=1$ and $y=0$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\nx+(0)+(1)=1\\,⟹\\,x=1-1=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=0$, $y=0$, and $z=1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $⟨0,0,1⟩.$"] [17592186235965 :answer/value "⟨0,1,1⟩"] [17592186236139 :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩"] [17592186236938 :answer/value "⟨1,1,1⟩"] [17592186237040 :answer/value "⟨1,0,1⟩"] [17592186237135 :answer/value "⟨0,0,1⟩"] [17592186097179 :question/problem "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [17592186097179 :question/worked-solution "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say,  ${x}_{1}$, ${x}